.TH OMX-PANEL 1 "2026-10-26" "omx-panel" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx-panel \- check a skin package for an OpenMixer plugin panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-panel
.B validate
.IR "skin.json | skin-package-directory" ...
.br
.B omx-panel
.B vocabulary
.RI [ package / name ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B omx-panel validate
reads each skin given, a
.I skin.json
file or a directory holding one, and checks it against the skin package schema shipped with the package. Each skin prints one line: its path and whether it is valid, with the first problem found when it is not.
.PP
.B omx-panel vocabulary
reads each installed source a panel is laid out by and prints one line for each, where it was read from:
the contract directories, omx-contract's meanings, plugin-hostd's LV2 unit table, the param-contract header,
and the descriptor of each
.IR package / name
given. A line starts with
.B ok
or, for a source that is not installed,
.BR FAIL .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
every skin is valid; every source is read
.TP
.B 1
at least one skin is not valid; a source is not installed
.TP
.B 2
usage error, or a file could not be read
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OMX_CONTRACT_PATH
a
.B :
list of contract directories, read in place of the installed one; the first that holds a package is the one read
.TP
.B OMX_CONTRACT_SCHEMA
an omx-contract.schema.json read in place of the installed one
.TP
.B PLUGIN_HOSTD_TABLES
a directory holding lv2.json, read in place of plugin-hostd's installed one
.TP
.B OMX_PARAM_CONTRACT_H
an omx_param_contract.h read in place of the installed one
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/omx-panel/schema/skin-package.schema.json
the schema a skin is checked against
.TP
.I /usr/share/omx-contract/contract.d
the contract directory, where no
.B OMX_CONTRACT_PATH
is set and pkg-config has no omx-contract (omx-contract-data installs it; omx-contract-devel adds the pkg-config file)
.TP
.I /usr/share/omx-contract/omx-contract.schema.json
the meanings a descriptor's controls play
.SH SEE ALSO
The skin package format, the panel description and the MOD GUI generator are documented in
.IR /usr/share/doc/omx-panel/ .
